{"ticker":"GRAPHITE","symbol":"GRAPHITE","instrumentId":3022922,"name":"Graphite India","industry":"NSE-Electrical-Power/Equipmt","about":"Graphite India Ltd. (GIL) is a pioneer in the manufacturing of carbon and graphite products, with a history dating back to the 1960s. Initially focused on graphite electrodes, the company has expanded into specialty carbon and graphite applications. Leveraging its core competencies and economies of scale, GIL efficiently enhances its production capacity to meet global demand. With manufacturing facilities strategically located near inland customers and seaports, GIL ensures timely deliveries worldwide. The company's commitment to consistent quality has earned it a strong reputation in the global market. In addition to graphite, GIL also manufactures high-speed steel, alloy steel, and glass-reinforced plastic pipes.","website":"www.graphiteindia.com","location":"Kolkata, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:23:40.237Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":785.25,"changePct":0.3514376996805112,"week52High":851.2,"week52Low":526.15},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹15,342 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹3,126 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"68,381,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"217"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"34,729,282"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.89%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"2.62"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"2"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.17"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.35"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-8%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"65.99"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"11–83"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"3.0%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"4.22"},{"label":"Volume","value":"433,363"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"2,087,167"},{"label":"Master score","value":"58"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"43"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"79"},{"label":"Group rank